// pixar-ad takes ANY animated-film-look ask at ANY length. There is no
// quick tier that routes elsewhere, and that is the mistake its description
// exists to prevent.
{"intent":"a spot where a sad little mattress comes to life and finds a friend","expected_skill":"pixar-ad"}
{"intent":"make our mascot the hero of a thirty second story with narration over it","expected_skill":"pixar-ad"}
{"intent":"a disney looking short about the problem our app solves","expected_skill":"pixar-ad"}
{"intent":"cute 3D characters, warm lighting, an emotional end card with the logo","expected_skill":"pixar-ad"}
{"intent":"board it across five beats and render each beat from its own frame","expected_skill":"pixar-ad"}
// Indirect: names a feeling and a genre of film, never a technique.
{"intent":"I want people to tear up at the end, like those animated insurance ads","expected_skill":"pixar-ad"}
// Style unstated. Smooth 3D is the default read; clay has to be asked for, by
// name or by texture.
{"intent":"a cute animated character ad, whatever style looks best","expected_skill":"pixar-ad","ambiguous_with":["claymation-ad"]}
// "Quick" reads like the catch-all's single call and is not: there is no one-call
// tier here, so every animated length is still a storyboard with ffmpeg at the end.
{"intent":"just a quick animated one, fifteen seconds, nothing fancy","expected_skill":"pixar-ad","ambiguous_with":["novoads-api"]}
